{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/4u4kka","slideIndex":5,"text":"Demo question: Would you like to reopen this ticket or create a new ticket? A clear reopen choice calls reopenTicket with the actual saved ID. The Java tool validates a positive ID, reloads the ticket and permits only CLOSED status. It sets OPEN and saves inside a transaction. The existing JPA PreUpdate hook refreshes updatedOn to the current server time. createdOn, ownership, summary, issue type and priority remain unchanged. Choosing a new ticket follows proposal and final confirmation, and leaves the closed ticket unchanged. An ambiguous YES requires clarification. There is no reopen notification call in the current implementation.\n\nSource: helpdesk.st; TicketTools.java; TicketToolsImpl.java; Ticket.java"}
