{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/978k4c","slideIndex":6,"text":"Ticket has two many-to-one links to HelpdeskUsers: creator is required and assignee is optional at the entity level. Tool-based creation always resolves an assignee. JPA lifecycle hooks set createdOn and updatedOn. Chat memory stores at most 10 messages per conversation in process memory. HTTP session continuity requires the client to reuse its session cookie. Memory is lost on restart and does not authenticate a user.\n\nSource: Ticket.java; HelpdeskUsers.java; ChatMemoryConfig.java; TicketController.java"}
