{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/isj9i5","slideIndex":9,"text":"The dedicated reopenTicket tool now supports CLOSED to OPEN. The general updateTicket tool still has optional summary and priority parameters which are assigned unconditionally, so omitted values may overwrite stored data with null. Confirmation and duplicate prevention depend on prompt compliance, with no server-side confirmation state or duplicate constraint shown. No Spring Security dependency or authenticated ownership checks appear in the reviewed code. Fixed email recipients and email-before-commit can cause misleading delivery if persistence later rolls back. Configuration includes sensitive values that should move to external secrets. Do not expose them during the demo. The unused named executor does not control CompletableFuture.runAsync calls.\n\nSource: TicketTools.java; TicketToolsImpl.java; TicketServiceImpl.java; pom.xml; application.properties; ThreadPoolConfig.java"}
