{"kind":"table","id":"tb/pojudcfe","slideIndex":10,"position":{"left":64,"top":175,"width":1152,"height":420},"name":"","rows":6,"cols":2,"preview":"Tool name | What it does"}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/g40d3x","slideIndex":10,"text":"Registered through .tools(ticketTools, generalTool). createTicket: Creates an OPEN ticket and assigns support. reopenTicket: Changes CLOSED to OPEN and refreshes updatedOn. updateTicket: Updates summary and priority on an existing ticket. findTicketById: Loads one saved ticket by its exact ID. findTicketsBySummary: Finds literal summary matches for one creator. createTicket, reopenTicket and updateTicket require explicit user confirmation in their tool instructions. updateTicket currently assigns optional fields unconditionally. Summary search is literal and case-insensitive, not semantic search. Time tools use the server timezone. findTicketAssignedTo ranks fewest OPEN, then fewest INPROGRESS, then most total tickets, then lowest user ID. Lookup tools marked returnDirect=true may return ticket data directly.\n\nSource: TicketTools.java; GeneralTool.java; TicketToolsImpl.java; GeneralToolImpl.java"}
